1
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:34,250
techniques, measuring, essentially. Have you ever added too much pepper to a

2
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:38,370
recipe? I know, it's not so great afterwards, but it's an innocent mistake.

3
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:43,210
But in the lab, you have to be sure to have precise measurements. So we're going

4
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:52,530
to learn how to get those now. We'll be using the volumetric pipette, the

5
00:00:52,530 --> 00:01:04,440
burette, the volumetric flask, and the syringe. Now for some basic rules. First

6
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:09,880
and foremost, keep all glassware clean. You want to be able to clearly read the

7
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:16,120
markings on all your equipment. Therefore, keep it clean. Also, you always need to

8
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:20,720
read at the bottom of the meniscus. The meniscus is the curved interface between

9
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:25,480
the air and the liquid. You need to read at eye level and at the bottom of the

10
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:31,200
meniscus in order to get a correct reading. Now for the basics of washing

11
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:37,440
your equipment. First, use soap solution to clean it. Then rinse with tap water.

12
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:43,720
Then rinse with distilled water, rinsing thoroughly each time. Finally, rinse with

13
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:55,610
solvent, if appropriate, and let dry. Now let's cover the equipment. Pipettes are

14
00:01:55,610 --> 00:02:01,450
used to measure small quantities of volume, usually up to 10 milliliters. They

15
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:06,610
work on the principle of creating a vacuum. Notice the pipette's gradation

16
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:13,210
marks. Now let's learn all about the bulb. Here is the bulb of a volumetric

17
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:20,090
pipette. Squeeze A and then squeeze this section of the bulb and you'll

18
00:02:20,090 --> 00:02:27,250
create a vacuum. If you want to suction up liquid, squeeze S. If you want to expel

19
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:36,860
liquid, squeeze E. Here's a demonstration of creating and then releasing the

20
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:47,720
vacuum. Caution! Never use your mouth to suction up liquids. Now for some basic

21
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:55,330
pipetting. First, you need to create a vacuum. Squeeze A and push in the bulb to

22
00:02:55,330 --> 00:03:07,830
do this. To draw up liquid, squeeze S. There it goes. And to expel your liquid,

23
00:03:07,830 --> 00:03:19,300
you then want to squeeze E. Down it goes. When you're all done, squeeze A

24
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:29,010
again to release the vacuum. Now for filling a pipette. First, create a vacuum.

25
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:37,010
Then draw up past the zero mark. This is to coat the interior walls. Then expel

26
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:43,010
all your liquid. Draw up past the zero mark once again, but this time slowly

27
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:49,870
release to the zero mark. Or you may choose to slowly draw up to the zero

28
00:03:49,870 --> 00:04:00,340
mark instead. Caution! Never allow any liquid to enter the bulb. Finally,

29
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:05,140
cleaning the pipette. You want to rinse with soap and water and solvent as

30
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:14,650
usual, but remember, don't get anything in the bulb. Volumetric flasks are used to

31
00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:23,330
dilute solutions. What would we need for this process? The flask, powder, or

32
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:28,890
concentrated solution instead. A funnel and stirring rod for guiding in the

33
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:36,030
solution, solvent for rinsing, solvent for pouring in and diluting, and finally a

34
00:04:36,030 --> 00:04:41,850
pipette to add the last drops up to the gradation mark. If you're going to make

35
00:04:41,850 --> 00:04:48,210
a solution from powder, uncap the flask and add your weighed powder into the

36
00:04:48,210 --> 00:04:55,480
flask carefully. Alternatively, you may choose to use concentrated solution

37
00:04:55,480 --> 00:05:00,240
instead. Use a funnel and possibly a stirring rod to guide the solution into

38
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:08,950
the flask. Now it's very important that you rinse with the appropriate solvent. In

39
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:14,870
our case, we're diluting with water, but you may be using something else. Be sure

40
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:23,920
to rinse the beaker, the stirring rod, and the funnel three times each. Add these

41
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:38,070
washings directly to the flask. Now for adding the solvent. Take your solvent

42
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:50,510
and fill the flask half full. Swirl or invert to facilitate dissolution. Then add

43
00:05:50,510 --> 00:06:01,380
more solvent, but be sure not to fill to the gradation mark. Notice here how we

44
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:06,920
didn't fill it up to the mark. Let the flask sit to allow drainage from the

45
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:17,650
interior walls. Important! Make sure your solute is completely dissolved. Here is

46
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:22,930
some undissolved solute. Make sure you swirl and invert to dissolve this before

47
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:27,730
you continue with your dilution. After you know all is dissolved and you've

48
00:06:27,730 --> 00:06:32,350
allowed one minute for drainage, use a pipette to add the last few drops of

49
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:43,820
solvent up to the gradation mark. And finally, be sure to swirl or invert.

50
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:47,940
You'll notice that the bottom of the meniscus lines up with the gradation

51
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:56,110
mark. Now for storage. Use a clean dry storage bottle. You may choose to rinse it

52
00:06:56,110 --> 00:07:01,150
with a small amount from the flask. Swirl and invert the flask to make sure it's

53
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:10,700
all dissolved. Then pour it into the storage bottle. Be sure to cap firmly

54
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:19,940
before setting aside. Finally, cleaning the flask. Wash with soap and water as

55
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:28,180
usual. And if desired, clamp upside down to facilitate drying. Burettes are used

56
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:33,820
to measure and precisely dispense small quantities as seen here in titrations.

57
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:41,350
Let's address the proper hand position. Wrap your hand around the burette as

58
00:07:41,350 --> 00:07:45,990
shown. Gently pushing forward the top portion with your forefinger allows

59
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:50,830
titrant to flow. Gently pushing forward the bottom portion with your middle

60
00:07:50,830 --> 00:08:01,120
finger seizes the flow of titrant. Now for filling the burette. Here is your

61
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:12,910
titrant. Take your burette and add a few milliliters of titrant to it. Then tilt

62
00:08:12,910 --> 00:08:18,790
and rotate your burette to coat the interior walls with titrant. Allow all

63
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:29,600
the titrant to drain out. Then fill your burette to above the zero mark. But

64
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:37,250
wait, we need to get rid of air bubbles. So what's wrong with this burette? Well,

65
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:42,050
you guessed it, there are air bubbles in the tip. This could be a major problem.

66
00:08:42,050 --> 00:08:46,970
To get rid of air bubbles, quickly rotate the valve back and forth, allowing small

67
00:08:46,970 --> 00:08:52,010
amounts of liquid to pass through intermittently. Look, no more air

68
00:08:52,010 --> 00:08:58,210
bubbles. Now that they're gone, we can proceed to drain the burette. Remember,

69
00:08:58,210 --> 00:09:03,130
you filled it to above the zero mark. Now you'll slowly drain it to the zero

70
00:09:03,130 --> 00:09:08,690
mark, but you don't have to reach it exactly. Just make sure you record the

71
00:09:08,690 --> 00:09:14,570
starting value, regardless of where it is, before you do anything else. Now let's

72
00:09:14,570 --> 00:09:19,810
learn about proper meniscus reading. Remember to read at the bottom of the

73
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:25,090
meniscus and to avoid parallax, which is inaccurate reading, always read at eye

74
00:09:25,090 --> 00:09:32,370
level. Here, the burette can easily be read as 3.50 milliliters. But what

75
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:38,570
happens if you read from below? Well, it's 3.55 milliliters, more than the

76
00:09:38,570 --> 00:09:47,050
actual amount. And if we read from above, it appears as 3.45 milliliters,

77
00:09:47,050 --> 00:09:54,050
less than the actual amount. Moral of the story, avoid parallax and read at eye

78
00:09:54,050 --> 00:10:04,940
level. Now, cleaning the burette. Use a long burette brush, as shown here. Wash

79
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:09,620
with soap and water, as usual, and make sure that you wash through the tip.

80
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:18,760
Syringes are used to measure and transfer very small quantities, such as

81
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:27,210
those in microliters. So let's explore transfer via the syringe. Take your

82
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:32,690
syringe, and with the curved needle, as shown here, draw up more solution than

83
00:10:32,690 --> 00:10:39,130
you actually need. You have an air bubble in your barrel. Tap it until it reaches

84
00:10:39,130 --> 00:10:48,820
the top. There's the air bubble at the top. Now expel some solution until you

85
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:54,100
get to the amount that you actually need. After you expel some of the

86
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:57,940
solution, you've pushed out the air. So your needle is entirely full of

87
00:10:57,940 --> 00:11:03,100
solution, and there should be a little drop at the end. In order not to lose

88
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:09,260
anything from the needle, you need to withdraw a cushion of air. Now you're

89
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:16,100
ready for transfer. Transfer the solution to the receiving vessel. But

90
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:20,420
wait! Even though you think you've transferred it all, you still have liquid

91
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:26,620
in your needle. You need to expel this excess liquid. Invert your syringe, and

92
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:31,220
by withdrawing and releasing the plunger, get rid of the excess liquid

93
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:38,950
by pushing it out. Finally, cleaning the syringe. Before washing, disassemble the

94
00:11:38,950 --> 00:11:45,430
syringe into its components. Needle, barrel, and plunger. Wash with soap and water

95
00:11:45,430 --> 00:11:55,780
separately. Rinse with solvent, and allow to dry. Now that you have the skills, go

96
00:11:55,780 --> 00:12:02,300
forth and measure. Remember, this video is intended to help you prepare for lab

97
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:07,580
by providing a demonstration of the proper experimental technique. It is not

98
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:11,660
intended as a replacement for reading your lab manual or the supplementary

99
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:16,460
material. In order to become a great experimentalist, it is important that you

100
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:23,020
understand both theory and technique. Now it's your turn. Good luck!
